-5c33-85d4-d5b82c87f855" :question/math-academy-id "q-8006" :question/problem "Calculate the points where the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=12$ intersects the line $x=-4.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $x=-4,$ we substitute $x=-4$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =12 \\\\ (-4)^{2}-{y}^{2} & =12 \\\\ 16-{y}^{2} & =12 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =12-16 \\\\ -{y}^{2} & =-4 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the vertical line $x=-4$  at the points $(-4,\\pm 2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-8006/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "395f435d-473f-5dae-b215-2986556d5793"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8006"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-84056"] :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $14{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}=50$ intersects the line $y=2x.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=2x,$ we first replace $y$ with $2x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2} & =50 \\\\ 14{x}^{2}-3(2x)^{2} & =50 \\\\ 14{x}^{2}-12{x}^{2} & =50 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =50 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =25 \\\\ x & =\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-170559/selection/2d72fb9577d14e692ee0c494e42dfc349f511e1def3de9a4ad7e2ebebd23a09a" :answer/id #uuid "170c61dd-21b6-511d-9a0f-97f50a367351" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170559/selection/a869d0e88ffced7d6d9f6ba0e40ce1a27c2d4cababfdddf641f153f4e11398a6" :answer/id #uuid "3d2c3f17-3ec8-5e24-ac59-675d25152d16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm \\fra